# JavaScript & React

Ahentic uses **regular JavaScript** (`.js`), not TypeScript. Do not add `.ts` / `.tsx` source files for plugin UI or runtime code.

## Sidebar is the main workspace

- The **React sidebar** is the primary product surface (Cursor-like workspace), available on **wp-admin and the front-end** for users with `manage_options`.
- Expect a **JS-heavy** codebase under `src/admin/js/sidebar/`.
- Prefer putting interactive workspace logic in JS. PHP should expose REST/data/tools and bootstrap assets — not own the workspace UX.
- Keep React focused on rendering state; heavier agent/tool orchestration stays on the server (via php-ai-client and WordPress APIs) unless there is a clear client-side reason.

## React

- Build UI with **React** via `@wordpress/element` (WordPress’s React wrapper), same pattern as Cimo.
- Use JSX inside `.js` files (wp-scripts handles transpilation).
- Prefer WordPress packages (`@wordpress/element`, `@wordpress/components`, `@wordpress/i18n`, etc.) over adding a separate `react` / `react-dom` dependency.
- Icons: `lucide-react`.
- Mount UI with `createRoot` from `@wordpress/element` into `#ahentic-root`.

## Styling & theme

- All sidebar chrome styles are scoped under `.ahentic` so they do not fight WP admin / theme CSS.
- Visual tokens live on `[data-ahentic-theme="dark"]` (and future themes). Prefer tokens (`--ah-bg`, `--ah-fg`, …) over hard-coded colors in components.
- Default theme is dark. Do not assume a light theme exists yet.
- When open on desktop, the sidebar **pushes** page content via `--ahentic-sidebar-inset` (does not overlay content).

## Persistence

- **Browser `localStorage`** (`ahentic.sidebar.v1`): open/closed, width, theme, mode, open tabs, active tab id.
- **Not in the browser:** conversation message bodies — those will be saved in the database later. Keep messages in React memory for mocks only.
- Do not invent ad-hoc storage keys; extend the shared helpers in `src/admin/js/sidebar/storage.js`.

## Keyboard

- Toggle sidebar with `Cmd+L` (macOS) / `Ctrl+L` (Windows/Linux) on any page where the script is loaded.
